{
  "schema": 1,
  "meta": {
    "name": "guard",
    "description": "How pk guard protects branches - modes, the push policy, and how to change them"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "id": "pk-guard",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "pk guard"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Guard is a PreToolUse hook on shell commands. When the agent is about to run a git mutation ("
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "commit"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "merge"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "push"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "rebase"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "reset"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "), guard checks "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and answers with a permission decision. Two policies apply, and the strongest decision wins:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "type": "para",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "branch policy ("
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "guard.mode"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "): mutations while a protected branch ("
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "guard.branches"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ") is checked out are denied ("
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "block"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "), questioned ("
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "ask"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "), or ignored ("
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "off"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ")"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "para",
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "push policy ("
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "guard.push"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "): any "
              },
              {
                "type": "code",
                "text": "git push"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", on any branch, is denied, questioned, or ignored. Pushing is the developer's explicit action; commits stay local until you push them."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Guard recognizes git through chains ("
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "\u0026\u0026"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ";"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "|"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "), environment prefixes, absolute paths, "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "git -C"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", and "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": "git.exe"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", so a compound command is judged by its parts."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "what-guard-is",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "What guard is"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "A guardrail against an agent following its defaults, not a security boundary. Internal errors fail open with a note on stderr, and an unconfigured repository (no "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ") is always a no-op."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "id": "changing-policy",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Changing policy"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "para",
      "inlines": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Edit "
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "text": ".pk.json"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " and commit it; policy travels with the repository."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "codeblock",
      "lang": "json",
      "text": "\"guard\": { \"branches\": [\"main\"], \"mode\": \"block\", \"push\": \"block\" }\n"
    }
  ]
}
